SPECIFICATION.md-1-# Project: `pbnfc`, an eight-thread BNF compiler and markup recognizer
SPECIFICATION.md-2-
SPECIFICATION.md-3-Implement a self-contained ISO C11 command-line program that compiles a BNF
SPECIFICATION.md-4-grammar and recognizes hierarchical HTML-like documents. The recognizer must
SPECIFICATION.md:5:perform its parsing work through a persistent pool of exactly eight POSIX worker
SPECIFICATION.md-6-threads and deterministically combine their partial results. External parser
SPECIFICATION.md-7-generators and non-standard libraries are forbidden; POSIX `pthread` is allowed.
SPECIFICATION.md-8-
SPECIFICATION.md:9:This is not a file-splitting exercise. All eight workers cooperate on the chart
SPECIFICATION.md:10:for one document. A coordinator distributes chart items in parallel rounds,
SPECIFICATION.md:11:workers produce thread-local candidates, and the coordinator merges and
SPECIFICATION.md-12-deduplicates those candidates in a stable order before the next round.
SPECIFICATION.md-13-
SPECIFICATION.md-14-## Required interface
SPECIFICATION.md-15-
SPECIFICATION.md-16-`make clean all` must build `bin/pbnfc` with strict warnings and pthread support.
SPECIFICATION.md-17-
SPECIFICATION.md-18-```text
SPECIFICATION.md:19:bin/pbnfc --grammar PATH --input PATH [--start NAME] [--stats]
SPECIFICATION.md-20-```
SPECIFICATION.md-21-
SPECIFICATION.md-22-On recognition success, exit 0 and print:
SPECIFICATION.md-23-
SPECIFICATION.md-24-```text
SPECIFICATION.md-25-ACCEPT tokens=N
SPECIFICATION.md-26-```
SPECIFICATION.md-27-
SPECIFICATION.md:28:With `--stats`, append these fields on the same line:
SPECIFICATION.md-29-
SPECIFICATION.md-30-```text
SPECIFICATION.md:31:workers=8 active_workers=8 rounds=N tasks=N,N,N,N,N,N,N,N
SPECIFICATION.md-32-```
SPECIFICATION.md-33-
SPECIFICATION.md-34-Every task count must be positive for the supplied stress document. `rounds`
SPECIFICATION.md:35:must be positive. Without `--stats`, output must be deterministic and contain
SPECIFICATION.md-36-no timing or scheduling-dependent values.
SPECIFICATION.md-37-
SPECIFICATION.md-38-For a syntactically valid grammar with rejected markup, exit 1 and print one
SPECIFICATION.md-39-line beginning `REJECT ` with decimal byte `offset=`, `line=`, and `column=`
--
SPECIFICATION.md-98-
SPECIFICATION.md-99-## Required eight-thread parser architecture
SPECIFICATION.md-100-
SPECIFICATION.md-101-Use a safe general chart recognizer, such as Earley recognition. Create exactly
SPECIFICATION.md:102:eight worker pthreads once per process and reuse them until parsing ends.
SPECIFICATION.md-103-
SPECIFICATION.md-104-For each chart position and fixed-point closure wave:
SPECIFICATION.md-105-
SPECIFICATION.md-106-1. The coordinator snapshots the current unprocessed item range and partitions
SPECIFICATION.md:107:   it across all eight workers.
SPECIFICATION.md-108-2. Workers perform prediction/completion work and write only to their own
SPECIFICATION.md-109-   candidate vectors; shared grammar and chart snapshots are read-only.
SPECIFICATION.md-110-3. A barrier or condition-variable generation protocol returns control to the
SPECIFICATION.md-111-   coordinator.
--
SPECIFICATION.md-113-   candidates, merges duplicates, appends new items, and repeats until closure.
SPECIFICATION.md-114-5. Scanning work is likewise distributed through the pool, with next-position
SPECIFICATION.md-115-   candidates combined deterministically.
SPECIFICATION.md-116-
SPECIFICATION.md:117:All workers must perform real chart work on the stress case. Protect lifecycle
SPECIFICATION.md-118-state with mutexes/condition variables or barriers, handle allocation failures,
SPECIFICATION.md-119-join all threads on every normal/error exit, and avoid data races. Do not create
SPECIFICATION.md-120-a new set of threads for every token or chart item. The coordinator is not one
SPECIFICATION.md:121:of the eight reported workers.
